  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::BookDefinition
  book_index: 11
  book_title: Strange Tales of Plants
  book_color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  book_clue_index: 112
  content: 
  clue_content: "(One page caught my attention.)\n\nMoltshell Flower: A dark brown
    flower with slender stems and tiny buds, reportedly capable of changing shape
    on its own. Some claim to have seen its petals slowly curl backward after nightfall,
    revealing several long, curved filaments. In this state, it resembles a small
    insect with spindly legs.\n\n(Someone had scrawled a note beneath the entry)\n\u201CI
    figured it out! This isn\u2019t a flower at all!! I found proof in another book!
    It\u2019s a Heartbinder insect\u2014a creature used in witchcraft!\u201D"
